Smart Tool does not bundle third-party code. The installer downloads the components below from their official
sources into the installation folder or the user's profile; each keeps its own license.

Python packages (installation venv, from PyPI)
- ddgs (MIT)
- trafilatura (Apache-2.0)
- pystray (LGPL-3.0; used unmodified as a library)
- Pillow (MIT-CMU)
- PyYAML (MIT)

Browser runtime (web_adapters/browser/.venv, from PyPI and the projects' download servers)
- camoufox Python package (MIT) and the Camoufox browser, a Firefox fork (MPL-2.0), fetched by `camoufox fetch`
- Moli (Apache-2.0 OR MIT), https://github.com/lexmount/moli: renders JavaScript pages for web_fetch; downloaded at install time from its GitHub release (SHA-256 checked), with its own license files
- crawl4ai (Apache-2.0), https://github.com/unclecode/crawl4ai: page rendering is powered by Crawl4AI
- Playwright (Apache-2.0) and the Chromium build it installs (BSD-style, see https://www.chromium.org)

Node runtime and packages (web_adapters/node, from nodejs.org and npm)
- Node.js, downloaded only when no supported Node is installed (MIT and bundled licenses)
- open-websearch (Apache-2.0)
- typescript (Apache-2.0)
- java-parser (Apache-2.0)
- @angular/compiler (MIT)
- their dependencies as pinned in web_adapters/node/package-lock.json (MIT, ISC, BSD and Apache-2.0)

Web search sources
Smart Tool queries public search engines and APIs (DuckDuckGo, Yahoo, Wikipedia, Exa, Parallel, Keenable, Google and
Startpage through a local browser, and optionally Tavily and Firecrawl with your own key). Using them is subject to
each service's terms of use; free tiers are rate limited per IP address.
